# PantryMind — copy to .env and fill in. Never commit .env.

# ---- AWS ----
AWS_REGION=us-east-1
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# ---- Bedrock ----
# #22 (Bedrock Agent) is descoped — see CORRECTION 2026-08-18 below. Left blank;
# ConverseResponder (BEDROCK_CHAT_MODEL_ID below) is the production path.
BEDROCK_AGENT_ID=
BEDROCK_AGENT_ALIAS_ID=
# Titan Text Embeddings V2 outputs 1024 dims — must match VECTOR(1024) in schema.sql
BEDROCK_EMBED_MODEL_ID=amazon.titan-embed-text-v2:0

# Chat/classification models — both need a cross-region inference profile ID,
# not a bare model ID (on-demand throughput isn't supported for these).
BEDROCK_CHAT_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0
BEDROCK_CLASSIFY_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0

# CORRECTION 2026-08-17: the note previously here claimed the sonnet profile
# above was "verified working." Re-tested directly (`aws bedrock-runtime converse
# --model-id us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-5-20250929-v1:0 ...`) and it currently
# fails: `ResourceNotFoundException: Model use case details have not been
# submitted for this account.` This is a one-time account-level Anthropic
# marketplace form, separate from the model-access toggle and separate from the
# inference-profile requirement — both of those are fine. ALL Anthropic models
# are blocked account-wide until this is submitted, including legacy ones
# (tried claude-3-haiku too — different error, deprecated, also unusable).
# There is a CLI path (`aws bedrock put-use-case-for-model-access --form-data
# <json>`) but it submits real business/use-case info about this AWS account,
# so it needs whoever owns that answer, not a guessed payload. Likely fixed via
# AWS Console → Bedrock → Model access, which prompts for this on first request
# for an Anthropic model. classify.ts and the chat responder are written and
# ready — they will work the moment this is submitted, no code change needed.
#
# RESOLVED 2026-08-18: Prajwal submitted the use-case form. Live-verified end to
# end — POST /api/chat resolves the user, recalls real memories, gets a real
# Claude reply, and classify.ts correctly writes new preferences back to
# memory_vectors (tested with a brand-new fact, not just seeded data). Both
# claude-sonnet-4-5 (chat) and claude-haiku-4-5 (classify) confirmed working
# directly via `aws bedrock-runtime converse`. No code changes were needed.

# CORRECTION 2026-08-17 (2): issue #22 (Bedrock Agent) has a second, separate
# blocker, purely IAM privilege, unrelated to the use-case-form above. The
# `pukhraj-pantrymind` IAM user CAN deploy Lambdas and call bedrock-agent:CreateAgent
# (confirmed by direct probe — a create-agent call failed on iam:PassRole, not on
# CreateAgent itself), but has no iam:CreateRole / PutRolePolicy / AttachRolePolicy,
# and iam:PassRole is scoped to a pre-existing allowlist that doesn't cover a new
# role. The Bedrock Agent needs an execution role with a bedrock.amazonaws.com
# trust policy, which does not exist yet in this account. Fix is two scripts, run
# in order by whoever has IAM write access (Prajwal or account root), then anyone:
#   scripts/create-bedrock-agent-role.sh   — one-time, needs IAM admin
#   scripts/create-bedrock-agent.sh        — creates the agent + action groups,
#                                             works for pukhraj-pantrymind once
#                                             the role above exists
# The three action-group Lambdas (agent/adapters/bedrock-lambda-adapter, deployed
# as pantrymind-{pantry,recipes,shopping-list}-agent-adapter) are already deployed
# and live-verified end-to-end against Prajwal's real Lambdas and real seeded data
# — this blocker is only the agent resource itself, not the Lambda side.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-08-18: scripts/create-bedrock-agent-role.sh doesn't fully hand
# off to scripts/create-bedrock-agent.sh as written. pukhraj-pantrymind's
# iam:PassRole allowlist is scoped to a pre-existing set of role names (confirmed
# by probe) and a brand-new role — even one Prajwal just created — isn't in it
# until that allowlist is separately widened, which needs another IAM edit only
# he can make. Rather than chase a third round of IAM grants, the ask is simpler:
# Prajwal runs scripts/create-bedrock-agent.sh himself, under the same credentials
# he used to create the role. No new AWS Console steps, no new policy authoring.
#
# CORRECTION 2026-08-18 (2) — #22 DESCOPED, not just blocked. Prajwal ran
# create-bedrock-agent.sh himself (past the PassRole gate above) and hit a hard
# AWS account-level wall instead: `AccessDeniedException: Bedrock Agents is in
# Maintenance Mode. New agent creation is not available for accounts without
# prior service usage.` Confirmed against AWS's own docs (agents-classic-
# maintenance-mode.html): Bedrock Agents ("Classic" as of this change) closed to
# any AWS account with zero prior Agents usage on 2026-07-30, no exception
# process. This account has never created one, so it's permanently locked out of
# CreateAgent regardless of IAM/role/adapter correctness — all of which were
# independently verified fine before this surfaced. The only path forward for a
# new account is Bedrock AgentCore, described everywhere as a full
# re-architecture (different API/SDK, agent orchestration, unified gateway), not
# a swap-in — not attempted given hours left before feature freeze.
#
# Closed as won't-fix (#22, see issue comment for full writeup). Ships instead:
# ConverseResponder (BEDROCK_CHAT_MODEL_ID below) — already the live production
# path, already carries the full judged behavior (cross-session memory recall,
# visibly changing recommendations) without the formal Agent resource. What's
# lost is native Bedrock-mediated tool-calling into the Lambda action groups;
# ConverseResponder compensates by pulling real pantry contents directly into
# context instead (see #55). agent/adapters/ and agent/config/action-groups.json
# stay in the repo as evidence and in case AgentCore migration is worth
# revisiting post-hackathon.

# ---- CockroachDB Cloud ----
# From `ccloud cluster sql pantrymind --output json` (Phase 1)
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:26257/pantrymind?sslmode=verify-full

# ---- CockroachDB Managed MCP Server ----
COCKROACH_MCP_URL=https://cockroachlabs.cloud/mcp
COCKROACH_MCP_API_KEY=

# ---- S3 ----
S3_BUCKET=pantrymind-demo-assets-361769562408

# ---- External recipe API ----
SPOONACULAR_API_KEY=

# ---- Demo ----
# Single hardcoded user for the demo; memory recall is scoped to this handle
DEMO_USER_HANDLE=demo
